{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-001-r1s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261119-001-r1s0\ntitle: Resolve two quotient bits per step in the combinational RV32M divider\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The baseline's 199.837 ns worst path crosses operand forwarding and the EX ALU on its way to data memory. The ALU computes signed and unsigned division and remainder in one cycle. A serial chain of quotient decisions is a plausible source of the measured 156-cell depth. Shortening that chain can raise the clock frequency for every CoreMark instruction at the existing cycle count.\nhypothesis: |\n  Implement DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU with one combinational radix-4 restoring divider. Convert the operands to unsigned magnitudes according to the operation and precompute D, 2D and 3D once at 34-bit precision. Consume the dividend two bits at a time, most significant pair first. At each of 16 steps, append the next pair to the partial remainder and compute the three trial differences in parallel. Use their borrow bits to select the largest multiple that fits, emit its two-bit quotient digit and select the corresponding difference as the next remainder. Digit zero passes the trial remainder through. Use mutually exclusive digit selects so selection adds no second subtract to the serial path.\n  At step k (counting from one), the dividend prefix has only 2k bits. Limit each trial subtraction to that width and disqualify a multiple if any of its higher bits are set. This bounds early carry chains and reduces LUT and routing demand. Restore the quotient sign from the operand sign XOR and the remainder sign from the dividend. Handle a zero divisor explicitly and preserve the RV32M signed overflow result. Keep the existing combinational ALU interface, multiplication and ALTOPS expressions.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 30\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: Replace the four real DIV/REM operator expressions with the shared, width-limited radix-4 network. Select quotient or remainder at its output and retain single-cycle EX forwarding for all four operations.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: Extend the existing exact-result checks for all four operations with dividends just below, at and above multiples of the divisor, top-bit-set divisors whose 3D exceeds 32 bits, and seeded full-width operand pairs. Compute signed reference quotients by truncation toward zero and remainders from the dividend minus quotient times divisor.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
