{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_119", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261119-003-r1s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261119-003-r1s2\ntitle: Predict direct branches with a synchronous block RAM indexed by the next fetch PC\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Fetch always selects PC+4. Since IF/ID is combinational, each taken\n  branch or jump resolved in EX discards one younger fetch opportunity.\n  Between the CoreMark markers the reference ISS executes 294,425 taken\n  conditional branches and 49,367 JALs. A scratch RTL prototype of the\n  predictor below completed the same ten iterations in 4,188,685 bracketed\n  cycles versus 4,491,485 at baseline, with both stall generators enabled\n  and all five CRCs matching. Gowin reported 5.218, 5.320 and 5.320 MHz.\n  The median gives 12.70 iterations/s, 4.79% above the 12.12 champion.\n  The prototype used one additional BSRAM and 157 additional logic cells.\n  At this cycle count, clearing the 4.6% threshold requires more than\n  5.3102 MHz, so placement remains the main uncertainty.\nhypothesis: |\n  On an accepted fetch, predict legal conditional branches from the high\n  bit of a 1,024-entry table of two-bit saturating counters. Drive the\n  synchronous block-RAM read address from bits [11:2] of the very same\n  next PC that the fetch register samples. This delivers the matching\n  counter during fetch without adding a pipeline stage. Predict JAL\n  taken. Compute the direct target once from the current PC and B or J\n  immediate. Select it only when predicted taken, word-aligned and in\n  the 1 MiB instruction RAM. Otherwise select PC+4, including for JALR.\n  Carry both the decision and the computed target into EX. A direction\n  mismatch on a valid advancing instruction triggers a correction to\n  the architectural successor. A hit lets the younger instruction enter\n  ID/EX immediately. Train from the registered outcome in EX/MEM.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Predecode legal BRANCH funct3 and JAL from raw imem_data. For those\n      instructions, add the signed B/J offset to the current PC. Use one\n\n…[1211 of 4283 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b6c52c90faf0921e]…\nect\n      only on a valid advancing mismatch, to the same successor reported\n      in RVFI pc_next. Preserve the misalignment trap and PC+4 link.\n      Carry the counter snapshot alongside the registered branch outcome.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Write the table once for each valid legal conditional branch in\n      EX/MEM using its PC, outcome and counter snapshot. Inhibit training\n      on reset. Feed the EX correction to the existing hazard and IF\n      redirect inputs. A dmem hold defers correction until EX advances,\n      when correction takes priority over imem wait or load-use hold.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Train a loop branch taken, then make it fall through with a store\n      at its predicted target. Hold an older memory operation in MEM as\n      the exit resolves and deassert imemReady on release. Check that\n      the fall-through retires once, the branch reports its resolved\n      successor, and only the architecturally executed stores reach dmem.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
